%% Plover sequence diagrams — signup + normal API call.
%% Regenerate SVG: npx --package=@mermaid-js/mermaid-cli mmdc -i seq-diagram.mmd -o seq-diagram.svg
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant E as Electron (Plover.app)
  participant K as keytar
  participant B as Browser
  participant S as Cloud Run (plover-server)
  participant G as Google OAuth
  participant F as Firestore
  participant M as Gemini API

  Note over E,M: Scenario 1 — First-launch signup

  E->>K: getPassword('plover_token')
  K-->>E: null
  E->>E: render SignupScreen
  E->>E: generate 32-byte state nonce (in memory)
  E->>B: shell.openExternal(/signup?state=nonce)
  B->>S: GET /signup?state=nonce
  S->>S: rememberState(nonce)
  S-->>B: 302 → Google consent
  B->>G: OAuth consent (openid email)
  G-->>B: 302 → /oauth/callback?code=..&state=nonce
  B->>S: GET /oauth/callback
  S->>G: exchange code, verify id_token
  G-->>S: { sub, email }
  S->>F: upsert users/{sub}
  S->>S: generate raw token, hash SHA-256
  S->>F: create tokens/{hash}
  S-->>B: 302 plover://auth?token=raw&state=nonce
  B->>E: plover:// deep link
  E->>E: verify state matches in-memory nonce
  E->>K: setPassword('plover_token', raw)
  E->>E: drop nonce, load main window

  Note over E,M: Scenario 2 — Normal API call

  E->>K: getPassword('plover_token')
  K-->>E: raw token
  E->>S: POST /api/decompose (X-Plover-Auth-Token)
  S->>S: authMiddleware — hash(token)
  S->>F: lookup tokens/{hash}
  F-->>S: { userId, revoked=false }

  alt token missing or revoked
    S-->>E: 401 Unauthorized
    E->>E: show re-signup screen
  else token valid
    S->>F: atomic increment rate_limits/{userId}_{route}_{yyyymmdd}
    alt counter over quota
      F-->>S: over limit
      S-->>E: 429 + Retry-After
      E->>E: toast "slow down"
    else within quota
      F-->>S: ok
      S->>M: generateContent(...)
      M-->>S: { functionCalls }
      S-->>E: 200 { subtasks }
    end
  end
